# Feature testing

Before marking work done, classify the change and add the appropriate tests.

## Change types

| Change | Required testing |
|--------|------------------|
| Pure logic (utils, parsers, cache helpers) | Unit test in `src/test/unit/` |
| Extension host (commands, IPC, services) | Integration test in `src/test/integration/` or unit test on extracted core |
| Webview UI only | Manual smoke checklist in the PR summary; automated checks still required |
| Bug fix | Regression test at the lowest feasible layer (prefer unit) |

## Mandatory checks

Run in order and fix failures before finishing:

```bash
npm run check:types && npm run lint && npm run test
```

If any `src/**/*.css` or `src/**/*.scss` file changed, also run `npm run lint:styles` (or use `npm run lint:all` instead of `npm run lint`).

## File conventions

- Unit: `src/test/unit/<module>.test.ts`
- Integration: `src/test/integration/<area>.test.ts`
- Import application code with **relative paths** (e.g. `../../webviews/utils/branches`) so compiled tests resolve at runtime
- Use Mocha `describe` / `it`; name tests after behavior, not implementation.
- Cover the happy path and at least one meaningful edge case per new public function.

## Mocks

- Never call the real Linear API in automated tests.
- Stub `LinearClient`, `GitClient`, or extract pure logic for unit testing.

## Manual smoke template (webview features)

Document briefly when UI cannot be automated yet:

1. **Setup** — Extension Development Host, workspace state
2. **Steps** — open panel, trigger action
3. **Expected** — observable outcome

## Do not skip tests

Once test scaffolding exists in this repo, do not claim missing infrastructure as a reason to skip automated tests for testable logic.
